This is a sample article for the first version of the blog. It shows how an opening, a short section, and a closing thought will look when published.

## A place to leave notes

Personal sites give small ideas somewhere to go. A half-page note about an animation, a sketch of a tool, or a lesson from a refactor can be useful long before it becomes a polished essay.

> A note is worth keeping if it helps you notice something you’ll use again.

## Starting with the essentials

A home page helps readers discover what’s new. An archive makes older notes easy to come back to. A good article page gives each idea a clear place to unfold.

- Leave enough room for code and images.
- Make the next thing to read easy to find.
- Keep the text comfortable to read on a phone.
